    "content": "Goal\n* Please move the last sentence to the beginning.\n\n* Please change all {{constant}} format to <<bold>>.\n\n* Please format 0, 1, 8 and 9 as {{constants}}.\n\n* Please remove the quotation marks in 'A “signal”'.\n\n* Please change \"When\" to \"Every time\".\n\n* Please change \"      °\" to \"　°\" (a full-width space), as leading ordinary spaces are ignored and cannot be used for indentation.\n\n* Please add \".\" after \"resets to 0\".\n\n* Please add \"except previously overloaded cells\" after \"(including diagonals)\".\n\n* Please change \"diagonals\" to \"horizontal, vertical and diagonal\". (Remember to remove \"s\" from \"diagonals\".)\n\n* Please insert the following paragraph immediately before \"Your task\":\n\nIf several cells overload simultaneously, they may be processed in any order and should give the same result.\n\nInput\n* Line 1: Please add \"space-separated\" after \"Two\".\n\n* Next H lines: Please add \"representing one row of the grid\" at the end.\n\n* Next line: Please add \"space-separated\" after \"Two\".\n\n* Next line: Please add \"the row and column indexes (0-based) of\" before \"the starting cell\".\n\nConstraints\n* Please change 50 to 10.\n\n* Please remove \"0 ≤ grid values ≤ 9\".\n\nStub generator\n* Please change 50 to W.\n\nTags\n* Please remove \"Chain Reaction\", \"Logic\" and \"Propagation\".\n\nCases\n* After updating the stub generator, please click \"TEST IN IDE\". You'll be notified that, in the \"No Overload\" test, each grid row contains more than W characters. Please change W to 3.\n\n* Each test and its validator should cover the *same scenario* with slightly different inputs and outputs. So, please convert each test into a pair of cases as described below.\n\n* Test 1: Revise the input to demonstrate more clearly the effect of an overload on both neighbouring and non-neighbouring cells:\n\n5 5\n00000\n08120\n07930\n06540\n00000\n2 2\n\n* Validator 1: Use the same input as above, except that the ring of digits surrounding the centre increases counter-clockwise.\n\n* Use the existing cases (excluding Wave Expansion and Complex Cascade) as follows:\n\n  • Test 2: Full Overload\n\n  • Test 3: Chain Reaction, modified so that R > C\n\n  • Test 4: Diagonal Chain, modify the grid so that W < H, make R < C (e.g. 0 2), and replace all 8s with 9s\n\n  • Test 5: No Overload, replace both 1s with 9s, and keep W > H and the starting cell at (0, 0)\n\n  • Test 6: Large Calm Zone, keep the starting cell at bottom-right corner\n\n* Create new Validators 2 to 6, each matching its respective test with slight variations.\n\n* Please use the code here ( https://pastebin.com/2Dc75k0J ) to generate two new pairs of cases:\n\n  • Test/Validator 7: H = W = 8\n\n  • Test/Validator 8: H = W = 10\n\nThanks.",
